Subject: [PATCH] Harden 5S monitoring photo uploads against active-content XSS
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The tasks/evidence upload route (PR #316) and the general evidence
download path were already fixed to stop trusting client-declared
MIME type, but two related routes were missed: the 5S checklist
"before" photo upload (monitoring/rounds/5s) and the "after" photo
upload on recheck (monitoring/rounds/[id]/recheck). Both accepted
any file whose client-reported file.type merely started with
"image/" and then stored that same client-declared value as both
the DB mime_type and the Supabase storage contentType.

image/svg+xml passes that prefix check, and SVG can embed <script>
that browsers execute when the file is opened directly — the same
stored-XSS class already fixed elsewhere for evidence uploads.

Add safeImageMimeType() to evidence-file-policy.ts: an explicit
allowlist of 4 raster MIME types (jpeg/png/webp/gif), rejecting
svg+xml and anything else. Wire it into both 5S upload routes in
place of the spoofable startsWith("image/") check and the
client-echoed contentType/mime_type values.

